## 3. Ingestion pipeline (the most important part – build and test this FIRST)

### 3.1 Folder layout
```
repo/
  pdfs/                         # I drop PDFs here (any subfolders allowed)
  profiles/                     # exam profile YAMLs (ssc_cgl_tier1.yaml, generic.yaml)
  overrides/                    # per-test manual fixes (JSON), merged after parsing
  ingest/                       # python package
    cli.py                      # `python -m ingest --all` or `--file pdfs/x.pdf`
    layout.py  parser.py  figures.py  sections.py  topics.py  validate.py  docs.py
    tests/ (pytest, with the sample PDF as a fixture)
  public/data/
    manifest.json               # list of all tests (small, loads fast)
    tests/<test_id>.json        # one file per test
    img/<test_id>/q012_stem.webp, q012_full.webp ...
  docs/tests/<test_id>.md       # auto-generated documentation per test
  src/                          # React app
```

### 3.2 Algorithm (deterministic)
1. **Open PDF**, iterate pages. For each page compute `text_len`. If `text_len < 150` and the page has a large image covering > 50 % of the page → mark as **ad page**, skip. Log it.
2. **Remove header/footer/watermark noise** by geometry and string rules from the profile: ignore words whose `top` < header_height (default ≈ 140 pt on a 842 pt page, calibrate from sample) and any line matching profile `noise_patterns` (e.g. `Adda247`, `GET IT ON`, `Google Play`, `Test Prime`, `Download`, page URLs). Page-1 title bar is parsed for metadata, then removed.
3. **Build a continuous stream of lines** across pages with `(page, top, bottom, x0, text, is_bold)`; bold detection from font name containing `Bold`.
4. **Segment questions** with `^Q\s*(\d{1,3})\s*[.)]` anchored at the left margin. Sanity-check numbering is strictly increasing by 1; report gaps/duplicates.
5. For each question block, extract:
   - **stem** = lines until the first option line,
   - **options** = lines matching `^\(?([a-dA-D])[\).]` (support `(a)`, `a)`, `A.`, and 4 or 5 options per profile). Continuation lines (no marker) append to the previous option,
   - **answer** = regex `Ans\.?\s*\(?([a-eA-E])\)?` anywhere in the block, **including at the top of the next page** (guaranteed by the continuous stream),
   - the **bounding boxes** of the whole block (possibly spanning two pages) and of the `Ans.` line (to exclude it from images).
6. **Render mode decision** (`render_mode`):
   - `text`: normal, trusted text.
   - `image_stem`: stem contains an embedded image, a detected table (`page.find_tables`/rect-line grid), math-garble heuristics (a line that is only digits/short token directly above/below another short token inside the same block; lines containing `√`, `²`, `³`, `⁴`, `∈`, `θ`, `sin`/`cos`/`tan` together with isolated numeric lines; fonts containing "Math"), or ≥ 5 consecutive very short lines. The stem is cropped as an image; **options remain text buttons**.
   - `image_full`: ≥ 2 options are empty/very short (≤ 1 char) OR images sit in the option area. The whole region (stem + figure + options) is cropped as one image and the app shows plain **A / B / C / D** buttons beneath it.
   - Optionally also store the cropped image for `text` questions with a `has_alt_image` flag so the user can toggle "view original" if the text looks wrong.
7. **Image cropping**: render the page region at ≥ 2.5× scale with `pypdfium2`, crop to the block bbox with a small padding, **exclude the `Ans.(x)` line**, and exclude header/footer. If a block spans two pages, crop both parts and stitch them vertically. Trim whitespace, convert to WebP (quality ~85), keep each image under ~120 KB. The faint watermark is acceptable.
8. **Passages**: detect `Directions (a-b)` blocks; store passage text (or image if complex) once in `passages[]` and reference by `passage_id` from each question in range.
9. **Metadata** from the title line via profile regex: exam name, date (`01 Oct 2026` → `2026-10-01`), shift if present (`Shift 1/2`). Generate `test_id` slug: `ssc-cgl-2026-10-01[-shift-1]`; if it already exists, append `-v2`.
10. **Sections**: assign by profile ranges; if the profile is `generic`, create one section "All questions".
11. **Topic tagging without AI**: `profiles/topics.yaml` holds keyword/regex → topic rules (e.g. `Article \d+|Fundamental Rights|Constitution` → Polity; `tangent|chord|circle|prism|cylinder` → Geometry/Mensuration; `coded|code language` → Coding-Decoding; `Master Address|candidate address` → Address Matching; synonym/antonym/idiom/one-word → Vocabulary; `Rearrange` → Para Jumbles; etc.). Unmatched → "Other". Topics are optional hints used for analytics.
12. **Duplicate detection**: normalized-text hash per question; mark `duplicate_of` when the same question exists in another test (so analytics can avoid double counting, and users can build "unique question" practice sets).
13. **Validation report** (`public/data/tests/<id>.report.json` and printed in the CLI): expected vs. found question count, missing answers, answer letter not in options, < 2 options in `text` mode, numbering gaps, empty stems, count of image questions, list of every question with a warning, and a **confidence score** per question (1.0 = clean text; lower when heuristics were triggered). The CLI exits non-zero only for fatal errors; warnings never block the build but are surfaced in the generated docs and in the app's "Test details" page.
14. **Overrides**: `overrides/<test_id>.json` can patch any field of any question (`answer`, `render_mode`, `stem`, `options`, `section`, `delete: true`, `note`). Applied after parsing and before writing output. Provide `python -m ingest --suggest-overrides` that prints a ready-to-edit skeleton for every low-confidence question.
15. **Incremental & idempotent**: skip PDFs whose SHA-256 hash is unchanged (store in `public/data/.ingest-cache.json`). Re-running must produce byte-identical output.
16. **Auto documentation**: for each test write `docs/tests/<test_id>.md` with headings: `# <Test title>`, `## Source`, `## Summary` (date, total questions, sections, counts of text/image questions, warnings), `## Sections` (table with ranges and counts), `## Topic distribution`, `## Warnings & manual review needed`, `## Answer key (compact table)`, `## Changelog`. Also regenerate a top-level `docs/INDEX.md` listing all tests.

