## 12. How to work (important)

Work in phases. **After each phase, stop, summarise what you built, list known limitations, and tell me exactly how to test it.** Do not move on until I say "next".

1. **Phase 1 – Ingestion core:** profile loader, line stream, question/option/answer parsing, ad-page skipping, validation report, pytest on the sample PDF. Print a table of all 100 questions with `render_mode`, answer and warnings.
2. **Phase 2 – Figures & image crops, passages, tables, math-garble detection, WebP output, overrides, docs generation, caching.**
3. **Phase 3 – App shell:** routing, theme, design system, Library, Test Details, data loading from `public/data`.
4. **Phase 4 – Exam engine:** timers, sections, palette, persistence/resume, scoring, results, review.
5. **Phase 5 – Practice mode, mascot, messages, gamification, sounds.**
6. **Phase 6 – History & analytics, notebooks, export/import, PDF/CSV reports.**
7. **Phase 7 – PWA/offline, accessibility pass, performance pass.**
8. **Phase 8 – GitHub Actions deploy, README/docs polish, e2e tests.**

If anything in this spec is ambiguous or conflicting, choose the most sensible option, state your assumption in one line, and continue. When you hit a limitation (e.g. a figure the heuristics can't classify), degrade gracefully (show the cropped image, add a warning) rather than failing.

